# Codebase Research Guide

When writing or updating articles, always verify details against the actual codebase.
NEVER invent features — document only what exists in the code.

## Source Codebases

| Codebase | Path | Purpose |
|----------|------|---------|
| Backend | `/home/vishnu-intain/Documents/Node-App/intain-markets-node-app/` | APIs, services, business logic |
| UI | `/home/vishnu-intain/Documents/Node-App/intain-markets-ui/src/` | Screens, components, constants |

## Where to Find What

### Status Values & Constants
- Backend: `api/settlement/rails.js` (settlement statuses)
- Backend: `api/dealOnBoarding.js` (deal statuses, field lists)
- Backend: `api/securitization/securitization.routes.js` (SEC constants)
- UI: `src/Constants/index.js` (all API paths, status constants)
- UI: `src/Constants/settlementChain.js` (blockchain chain config)
- UI: `src/Utils/settlementPartyUtils.js` (settlement flow types)

### UI Screens & Fields
- Containers: `src/Containers/` — one folder per module
- Components: `src/Components/` — shared UI components
- Routes: `src/Routers/RootRouter.js` — all routes by role
- Side nav: `src/Components/SideNavbar/SideNavbar.js`

### API Routes & Modules
- Route registry: `routes/index.js` (v1 + v2 mount points)
- Module folders: `api/{module}/` (each has routes, service, helpers)
- OpenAPI: `openapi/` folder for API documentation
- Architecture: `docs/rules/` for backend coding standards

